</section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwnA" aria-labelledby="History"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="History">History</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Shell_plc&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1" title="Edit section: History"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwnQ" aria-labelledby="Origins"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Origins">Origins</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Shell_plc&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2" title="Edit section: Origins"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-left" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwng"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:KITLV_-_26871_-_Kleingrothe,_C.J._-_Medan_-_Burning_of_natural_gases_at_an_oil_drilling_site,_presumably_at_Pangkalan_Brandan,_East_Coast_of_Sumatra_-_circa_1905.tif" class="mw-file-description" id="mwnw"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:KITLV_-_26871_-_Kleingrothe,_C.J._-_Medan_-_Burning_of_natural_gases_at_an_oil_drilling_site,_presumably_at_Pangkalan_Brandan,_East_Coast_of_Sumatra_-_circa_1905.tif" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/KITLV_-_26871_-_Kleingrothe%2C_C.J._-_Medan_-_Burning_of_natural_gases_at_an_oil_drilling_site%2C_presumably_at_Pangkalan_Brandan%2C_East_Coast_of_Sumatra_-_circa_1905.tif/lossy-page1-250px-thumbnail.tif.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="2651" data-file-height="1608" data-file-type="bitmap" height="152" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/KITLV_-_26871_-_Kleingrothe%2C_C.J._-_Medan_-_Burning_of_natural_gases_at_an_oil_drilling_site%2C_presumably_at_Pangkalan_Brandan%2C_East_Coast_of_Sumatra_-_circa_1905.tif/lossy-page1-500px-thumbnail.tif.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwoA"/></a><figcaption id="mwoQ">The oil well at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pangkalan_Brandan" title="Pangkalan Brandan" id="mwog">Pangkalan Brandan</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Sumatra" title="North Sumatra" id="mwow">North Sumatra</a>, is considered to be the origin of Royal Dutch Shell, c. 1905</figcaption></figure>
<figure class="mw-halign-left" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwpA"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Aurora_1914_Sydney_Harbour.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwpQ"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Aurora_1914_Sydney_Harbour.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Aurora_1914_Sydney_Harbour.jpg/250px-Aurora_1914_Sydney_Harbour.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="2667" data-file-height="3511" data-file-type="bitmap" height="197" width="150" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Aurora_1914_Sydney_Harbour.jpg/330px-Aurora_1914_Sydney_Harbour.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwpg"/></a><figcaption id="mwpw">Shell benzine for Sir Ernest Henry Shackleton, Antarctic Expedition 1915</figcaption></figure>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwqA"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:COLLECTIE_TROPENMUSEUM_Afscheepsteiger_Tarakan_14_TMnr_10010382.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwqQ"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:COLLECTIE_TROPENMUSEUM_Afscheepsteiger_Tarakan_14_TMnr_10010382.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/COLLECTIE_TROPENMUSEUM_Afscheepsteiger_Tarakan_14_TMnr_10010382.jpg/250px-COLLECTIE_TROPENMUSEUM_Afscheepsteiger_Tarakan_14_TMnr_10010382.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="700" data-file-height="444" data-file-type="bitmap" height="159" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/COLLECTIE_TROPENMUSEUM_Afscheepsteiger_Tarakan_14_TMnr_10010382.jpg/500px-COLLECTIE_TROPENMUSEUM_Afscheepsteiger_Tarakan_14_TMnr_10010382.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwqg"/></a><figcaption id="mwqw">Royal Dutch Petroleum dock in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dutch_East_Indies" title="Dutch East Indies" id="mwrA">Dutch East Indies</a> (now <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indonesia" title="Indonesia" id="mwrQ">Indonesia</a>), c. 1925</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwrg">The Royal Dutch Shell Group was created in April 1907 through the amalgamation of two rival companies: the Royal Dutch Petroleum Company (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dutch_language" title="Dutch language" about="#mwt93" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwrw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"langx","href":"./Template:Langx"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"nl"},"2":{"wt":"Koninklijke Nederlandse Petroleum Maatschappij"}},"i":0}}]}'>Dutch</a><span about="#mwt93">: </span><i lang="nl" about="#mwt93">Koninklijke Nederlandse Petroleum Maatschappij</i><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Dutch-language_text" about="#mwt93" id="mwsA"/>) of the Netherlands and The "Shell" Transport and Trading Company Limited of the United Kingdom.<sup about="#mwt97" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-beginnings_20-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"beginnings"}}'><a href="#cite_note-beginnings-20" id="mwsQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwsg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwsw">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwtA">]</span></span></a></sup> It was a move largely driven by the need to compete globally with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Standard_Oil" title="Standard Oil" id="mwtQ">Standard Oil</a>.<sup about="#mwt100" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Aftalion2001_21-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Aftalion2001"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Aftalion2001-21"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Aftalion2001-21" id="mwtg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwtw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwuA">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwuQ">]</span></span></a></sup> The merger was arranged by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armenians_in_the_United_Kingdom" title="Armenians in the United Kingdom" id="mwug">British-Armenian</a> oil magnate <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calouste_Gulbenkian" title="Calouste Gulbenkian" id="mwuw">Calouste Gulbenkian</a>, resulting in him emerging as a major shareholder of the newly formed company.<sup about="#mwt103" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-vassiliou2_22-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"vassiliou2"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-vassiliou2-22"}}'><a href="#cite_note-vassiliou2-22" id="mwvA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwvQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwvg">[</span>22<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwvw">]</span></span></a></sup> The Royal Dutch Petroleum Company was a Dutch company founded in 1890 to develop an oilfield in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pangkalan_Brandan" title="Pangkalan Brandan" id="mwwA">Pangkalan Brandan</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Sumatra" title="North Sumatra" id="mwwQ">North Sumatra</a>,<sup about="#mwt94" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMerrillees201560_23-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEMerrillees201560"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMerrillees201560-23"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Merrillees"},"2":{"wt":"2015"},"p":{"wt":"60"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMerrillees201560-23" id="mwwg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwww"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwxA">[</span>23<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwxQ">]</span></span></a></sup> and initially led by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jean_Baptiste_August_Kessler" title="Jean Baptiste August Kessler" id="mwxg">August Kessler</a>, Hugo Loudon, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henri_Deterding" title="Henri Deterding" id="mwxw">Henri Deterding</a>. The "Shell" Transport and Trading Company (the quotation marks were part of the legal name) was a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Kingdom_of_Great_Britain_and_Ireland" title="United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland" id="mwyA">British</a> company, founded in 1897 by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marcus_Samuel,_1st_Viscount_Bearsted" title="Marcus Samuel, 1st Viscount Bearsted" id="mwyQ">Marcus Samuel, 1st Viscount Bearsted</a>, and his brother <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samuel_Samuel" title="Samuel Samuel" id="mwyg">Samuel Samuel</a>.<sup about="#mwt106" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-history_24-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"history"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-history-24"}}'><a href="#cite_note-history-24" id="mwyw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwzA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwzQ">[</span>24<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwzg">]</span></span></a></sup> Their father had owned an antique company in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Houndsditch" title="Houndsditch" id="mwzw">Houndsditch</a>, London,<sup about="#mwt109" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Forsyth2011_25-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Forsyth2011"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Forsyth2011-25"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Forsyth2011-25" id="mw0A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw0Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw0g">[</span>25<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw0w">]</span></span></a></sup> which expanded in 1833 to import and sell seashells, after which the company "Shell" took its name.<sup about="#mwt112" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-beginnings_20-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"beginnings"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-beginnings-20"}}'><a href="#cite_note-beginnings-20" id="mw1A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw1Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw1g">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw1w">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt115" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Falola_26-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Falola"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Falola-26"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Falola-26" id="mw2A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw2Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw2g">[</span>26<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw2w">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt118" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-dy_27-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"dy"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-dy-27"}}'><a href="#cite_note-dy-27" id="mw3A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw3Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw3g">[</span>27<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw3w">]</span></span></a></sup></p> 

<p id="mw4A">For various reasons, the new firm operated as a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dual-listed_company" title="Dual-listed company" id="mw4Q">dual-listed company</a>, whereby the merging companies maintained their legal existence but operated as a single-unit partnership for business purposes. The terms of the merger gave 60 percent stock ownership of the new group to Royal Dutch, and 40 percent to Shell. Both became <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holding_company" title="Holding company" id="mw4g">holding companies</a> for <span title="Dutch-language text" about="#mwt119" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mw4w" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"nl"},"2":{"wt":"[[Bataafsche Petroleum Maatschappij]]"}},"i":0}}]}'><i lang="nl"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bataafsche_Petroleum_Maatschappij" title="Bataafsche Petroleum Maatschappij" class="mw-redirect">Bataafsche Petroleum Maatschappij</a></i></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Dutch-language_text" about="#mwt119" id="mw5A"/>, containing the production and refining assets, and Anglo-Saxon Petroleum Company, containing the transport and storage assets.<sup about="#mwt123" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Gerretson346_28-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Gerretson346"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Gerretson346-28"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Gerretson346-28" id="mw5Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw5g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw5w">[</span>28<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw6A">]</span></span></a></sup> National patriotic sensibilities would not permit a full-scale merger or takeover of either of the two companies.<sup about="#mwt124" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Gerretson346_28-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Gerretson346"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Gerretson346-28" id="mw6Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw6g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw6w">[</span>28<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw7A">]</span></span></a></sup> The Dutch company, <span title="Dutch-language text" about="#mwt120" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mw7Q" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"nl"},"2":{"wt":"Koninklijke Nederlandsche Petroleum Maatschappij"}},"i":0}}]}'><i lang="nl">Koninklijke Nederlandsche Petroleum Maatschappij</i></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Dutch-language_text" about="#mwt120" id="mw7g"/> at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Hague" title="The Hague" id="mw7w">The Hague</a>, was in charge of production and manufacture.<sup about="#mwt127" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Gerretson347_29-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Gerretson347"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Gerretson347-29"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Gerretson347-29" id="mw8A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw8Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw8g">[</span>29<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw8w">]</span></span></a></sup> The British <i id="mw9A">Anglo-Saxon Petroleum Company</i> was based in London, to direct the transport and storage of the products.<sup about="#mwt128" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Gerretson347_29-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Gerretson347"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Gerretson347-29" id="mw9Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw9g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw9w">[</span>29<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw-A">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt129" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-dy_27-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"dy"}}'><a href="#cite_note-dy-27" id="mw-Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw-g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw-w">[</span>27<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw_A">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mw_Q">In 1912, Royal Dutch Shell purchased the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rothschild_&amp;_Co" title="Rothschild &amp; Co" id="mw_g">Rothschilds</a>' <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bnito" title="Bnito" id="mw_w">Russian oil assets</a> in a stock deal. The Group's production portfolio then consisted of 53 percent from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Indies" title="East Indies" id="mwAQA">East Indies</a>, 29 percent from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russian_Empire" title="Russian Empire" id="mwAQE">Russian Empire</a>, and 17 percent from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romania" title="Romania" id="mwAQI">Romania</a>.<sup about="#mwt130" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-dy_27-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"dy"}}'><a href="#cite_note-dy-27" id="mwAQM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQU">[</span>27<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt133" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-30" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-30"}}'><a href="#cite_note-30" id="mwAQc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQk">[</span>30<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="3" id="mwAQs" aria-labelledby="20th_century"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="20th_century">20th century</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Shell_plc&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3" title="Edit section: 20th century"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAQw"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Ford_Shell_Fuel_Lkw_IMG_20180417_192801.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAQ0"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Ford_Shell_Fuel_Lkw_IMG_20180417_192801.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Ford_Shell_Fuel_Lkw_IMG_20180417_192801.jpg/250px-Ford_Shell_Fuel_Lkw_IMG_20180417_192801.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="3045" data-file-height="2283" data-file-type="bitmap" height="187" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Ford_Shell_Fuel_Lkw_IMG_20180417_192801.jpg/500px-Ford_Shell_Fuel_Lkw_IMG_20180417_192801.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAQ4"/></a><figcaption id="mwAQ8">Shell tank truck from 1926 based on a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Model_TT" title="Ford Model TT" id="mwARA">Ford Model TT</a></figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwARE">During the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_World_War" title="First World War" class="mw-redirect" id="mwARI">First World War</a>, Shell was the main supplier of fuel to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_Expeditionary_Force_(World_War_I)" title="British Expeditionary Force (World War I)" id="mwARM">British Expeditionary Force</a>.<sup about="#mwt136" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-autogenerated1_31-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"autogenerated1"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-autogenerated1-31"}}'><a href="#cite_note-autogenerated1-31" id="mwARQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwARU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARY">[</span>31<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARc">]</span></span></a></sup> It was also the sole supplier of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aviation_fuel" title="Aviation fuel" id="mwARg">aviation fuel</a> and supplied 80 percent of the British Army's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TNT" title="TNT" id="mwARk">TNT</a>.<sup about="#mwt137" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-autogenerated1_31-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"autogenerated1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-autogenerated1-31" id="mwARo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwARs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARw">[</span>31<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAR0">]</span></span></a></sup> It also volunteered all of its shipping to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_Admiralty" title="British Admiralty" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAR4">British Admiralty</a>.<sup about="#mwt138" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-autogenerated1_31-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"autogenerated1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-autogenerated1-31" id="mwAR8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASE">[</span>31<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwASM">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romanian_Campaign_(1916)" title="Romanian Campaign (1916)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwASQ">German invasion of Romania</a> in 1916 saw 17% of the group's worldwide production destroyed.<sup about="#mwt139" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-autogenerated1_31-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"autogenerated1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-autogenerated1-31" id="mwASU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASc">[</span>31<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASg">]</span></span></a></sup> In 1919, Shell took control of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mexican_Eagle_Petroleum_Company" title="Mexican Eagle Petroleum Company" id="mwASk">Mexican Eagle Petroleum Company</a> and in 1921 formed Shell-Mex Limited, which marketed products under the "Shell" and "Eagle" brands in the United Kingdom. During the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genoa_Conference_(1922)" title="Genoa Conference (1922)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwASo">Genoa Conference</a> of 1922 Royal Dutch Shell was in negotiations for a monopoly over Soviet oilfields in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baku" title="Baku" id="mwASs">Baku</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grozny" title="Grozny" id="mwASw">Grosny</a>, although the leak of a draft treaty led to breakdown of the talks.<sup about="#mwt142" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-32" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-32"}}'><a href="#cite_note-32" id="mwAS0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAS4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAS8">[</span>32<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATA">]</span></span></a></sup> In 1929, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shell_Chemicals" title="Shell Chemicals" id="mwATE">Shell Chemicals</a> was founded.<sup about="#mwt143" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-autogenerated1_31-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"autogenerated1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-autogenerated1-31" id="mwATI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwATM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATQ">[</span>31<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATU">]</span></span></a></sup> By the end of the 1920s, Shell was the world's leading oil company, producing 11 percent of the world's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crude_oil" title="Crude oil" class="mw-redirect" id="mwATY">crude oil</a> supply and owning 10 percent of its tanker tonnage.<sup about="#mwt144" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-autogenerated1_31-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"autogenerated1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-autogenerated1-31" id="mwATc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwATg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATk">[</span>31<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwATs">During the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spanish_Civil_War" title="Spanish Civil War" id="mwATw">Spanish Civil War</a> the company sold oil to the Nationalist side of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francisco_Franco" title="Francisco Franco" id="mwAT0">Francisco Franco</a>.<sup about="#mwt147" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-33" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-33"}}'><a href="#cite_note-33" id="mwAT4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAT8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUA">[</span>33<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-left" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAUI"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Куда_бы_вы_ни_поехали,_вы_можете_быть_уверены_в_Shell.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAUM"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Куда_бы_вы_ни_поехали,_вы_можете_быть_уверены_в_Shell.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/%D0%9A%D1%83%D0%B4%D0%B0_%D0%B1%D1%8B_%D0%B2%D1%8B_%D0%BD%D0%B8_%D0%BF%D0%BE%D0%B5%D1%85%D0%B0%D0%BB%D0%B8%2C_%D0%B2%D1%8B_%D0%BC%D0%BE%D0%B6%D0%B5%D1%82%D0%B5_%D0%B1%D1%8B%D1%82%D1%8C_%D1%83%D0%B2%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%8B_%D0%B2_Shell.jpg/250px-%D0%9A%D1%83%D0%B4%D0%B0_%D0%B1%D1%8B_%D0%B2%D1%8B_%D0%BD%D0%B8_%D0%BF%D0%BE%D0%B5%D1%85%D0%B0%D0%BB%D0%B8%2C_%D0%B2%D1%8B_%D0%BC%D0%BE%D0%B6%D0%B5%D1%82%D0%B5_%D0%B1%D1%8B%D1%82%D1%8C_%D1%83%D0%B2%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%8B_%D0%B2_Shell.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="800" data-file-height="601" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/%D0%9A%D1%83%D0%B4%D0%B0_%D0%B1%D1%8B_%D0%B2%D1%8B_%D0%BD%D0%B8_%D0%BF%D0%BE%D0%B5%D1%85%D0%B0%D0%BB%D0%B8%2C_%D0%B2%D1%8B_%D0%BC%D0%BE%D0%B6%D0%B5%D1%82%D0%B5_%D0%B1%D1%8B%D1%82%D1%8C_%D1%83%D0%B2%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%8B_%D0%B2_Shell.jpg/500px-%D0%9A%D1%83%D0%B4%D0%B0_%D0%B1%D1%8B_%D0%B2%D1%8B_%D0%BD%D0%B8_%D0%BF%D0%BE%D0%B5%D1%85%D0%B0%D0%BB%D0%B8%2C_%D0%B2%D1%8B_%D0%BC%D0%BE%D0%B6%D0%B5%D1%82%D0%B5_%D0%B1%D1%8B%D1%82%D1%8C_%D1%83%D0%B2%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%8B_%D0%B2_Shell.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAUQ"/></a><figcaption id="mwAUU">1932 Shell advertisement poster by the British surrealist painter <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_Nash_(artist)" title="Paul Nash (artist)" id="mwAUY">Paul Nash</a></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAUc">Located in the north bank of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River_Thames" title="River Thames" id="mwAUg">River Thames</a> in London, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shell_Mex_House" title="Shell Mex House" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAUk">Shell Mex House</a> was completed in 1931, and was the head office for Shell's marketing activity worldwide.<sup about="#mwt148" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-autogenerated1_31-6" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"autogenerated1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-autogenerated1-31" id="mwAUo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAUs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUw">[</span>31<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAU0">]</span></span></a></sup> In 1932, partly in response to the difficult economic conditions of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Depression" title="Great Depression" id="mwAU4">Great Depression</a>, Shell-Mex merged its UK marketing operations with those of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BP" title="BP" id="mwAU8">BP</a> (British Petroleum) to create <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shell-Mex_&amp;_BP" title="Shell-Mex &amp; BP" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAVA">Shell-Mex &amp; BP</a>,<sup about="#mwt149" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-34" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-34"}}'><a href="#cite_note-34" id="mwAVE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAVI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVM">[</span>34<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVQ">]</span></span></a></sup> a company that traded until the brands separated in 1975. Royal Dutch Company ranked 79th among United States corporations in the value of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_War_II" title="World War II" id="mwAVU">World War II</a> military production contracts.<sup about="#mwt150" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-35" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-35"}}'><a href="#cite_note-35" id="mwAVY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAVc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVg">[</span>35<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAVo"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Shell_petrol_pump_1952.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAVs"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Shell_petrol_pump_1952.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Shell_petrol_pump_1952.jpg/250px-Shell_petrol_pump_1952.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="1837" data-file-height="3326" data-file-type="bitmap" height="344" width="190" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Shell_petrol_pump_1952.jpg/500px-Shell_petrol_pump_1952.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element mw-file-upright" style="--mw-file-upright: 0.75" id="mwAVw"/></a><figcaption id="mwAV0">Vintage petrol pump (1952)</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAV4">The 1930s saw Shell's Mexican assets seized by the local government.<sup about="#mwt151" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-autogenerated1_31-7" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"autogenerated1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-autogenerated1-31" id="mwAV8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAWA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWE">[</span>31<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWI">]</span></span></a></sup> After the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/German_invasion_of_the_Netherlands" title="German invasion of the Netherlands" id="mwAWM">invasion of the Netherlands</a> by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nazi_Germany" title="Nazi Germany" id="mwAWQ">Nazi Germany</a> in 1940, the head office of the Dutch companies was moved to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curaçao" title="Curaçao" id="mwAWU">Curaçao</a>.<sup about="#mwt152" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-autogenerated1_31-8" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"autogenerated1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-autogenerated1-31" id="mwAWY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAWc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWg">[</span>31<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWk">]</span></span></a></sup> In 1945, Shell's Danish headquarters in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Copenhagen" title="Copenhagen" id="mwAWo">Copenhagen</a>, at the time being used by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gestapo" title="Gestapo" id="mwAWs">Gestapo</a>, was bombed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Air_Force" title="Royal Air Force" id="mwAWw">Royal Air Force</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/De_Havilland_Mosquito" title="De Havilland Mosquito" id="mwAW0">De Havilland Mosquitoes</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Carthage" title="Operation Carthage" id="mwAW4">Operation Carthage</a>.<sup about="#mwt155" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-36" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-36"}}'><a href="#cite_note-36" id="mwAW8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAXA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXE">[</span>36<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAXM">In 1937, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iraq_Petroleum_Company" title="Iraq Petroleum Company" id="mwAXQ">Iraq Petroleum Company</a> (IPC), 23.75 percent owned by Royal Dutch Shell plc,<sup about="#mwt158" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-RLA_37-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"RLA"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-RLA-37"}}'><a href="#cite_note-RLA-37" id="mwAXU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAXY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXc">[</span>37<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXg">]</span></span></a></sup> signed an oil concession agreement with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muscat_and_Oman" title="Muscat and Oman" id="mwAXk">Sultan of Muscat</a>. In 1952, IPC offered financial support to raise an armed force that would assist the Sultan in occupying the interior region of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oman" title="Oman" id="mwAXo">Oman</a>, an area that geologists believed to be rich in oil. This led to the 1954 outbreak of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jebel_Akhdar_War" title="Jebel Akhdar War" id="mwAXs">Jebel Akhdar War</a> in Oman that lasted for more than 5 years.<sup about="#mwt161" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-OmansInsurgencies_38-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"OmansInsurgencies"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-OmansInsurgencies-38"}}'><a href="#cite_note-OmansInsurgencies-38" id="mwAXw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAX0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAX4">[</span>38<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAX8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-left" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAYA"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Tankstationmijnsheerenland.png" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAYE"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Tankstationmijnsheerenland.png" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Tankstationmijnsheerenland.png/250px-Tankstationmijnsheerenland.png" decoding="async" data-file-width="684" data-file-height="515" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Tankstationmijnsheerenland.png/500px-Tankstationmijnsheerenland.png 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAYI"/></a><figcaption id="mwAYM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Dutch_Shell" title="Royal Dutch Shell" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAYQ">Royal Dutch Shell</a> filling station and garage in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mijnsheerenland" title="Mijnsheerenland" id="mwAYU">Mijnsheerenland</a>, the Netherlands, late-1970s</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAYY">Around 1952, Shell was the first company to purchase and use a computer in the Netherlands.<sup about="#mwt163" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-39" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-39"}}'><a href="#cite_note-39" id="mwAYc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAYg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYk">[</span>39<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYo">]</span></span></a></sup> The computer, a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferranti_Mark_1" title="Ferranti Mark 1" id="mwAYs">Ferranti Mark 1</a>*, was assembled and used at the Shell laboratory in Amsterdam. In 1970, Shell acquired the mining company <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BHP#Billiton" title="BHP" id="mwAYw">Billiton</a>, which it subsequently sold in 1994.<sup about="#mwt166" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-40" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-40"}}'><a href="#cite_note-40" id="mwAY0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAY4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAY8">[</span>40<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAZE">In 1989, Shell redesigned a $3-billion natural gas platform in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Sea" title="North Sea" id="mwAZI">North Sea</a>, raising its height one to two meters, to accommodate an anticipated <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_level_rise" title="Sea level rise" id="mwAZM">sea level rise</a> due to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Climate_change" title="Climate change" id="mwAZQ">global warming</a>.<sup about="#mwt169" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-41" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-41"}}'><a href="#cite_note-41" id="mwAZU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZc">[</span>41<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAZk">In the 1990s, protesters criticised the company's environmental record, particularly the possible pollution caused by the proposed disposal of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brent_Spar" title="Brent Spar" id="mwAZo">Brent Spar</a> platform into the North Sea. Despite support from the UK government, Shell reversed the decision under public pressure but maintained that sinking the platform would have been environmentally better.<sup about="#mwt171" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-42" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-42"}}'><a href="#cite_note-42" id="mwAZs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZ0">[</span>42<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZ4">]</span></span></a></sup> Shell subsequently published an unequivocal commitment to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sustainable_development" title="Sustainable development" id="mwAZ8">sustainable development</a>, supported by executive speeches reinforcing this commitment.<sup about="#mwt174" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-43" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-43"}}'><a href="#cite_note-43" id="mwAaA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAaE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAaI">[</span>43<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAaM">]</span></span></a></sup> Shell was subsequently criticised by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_Commission" title="European Commission" id="mwAaQ">European Commission</a> and five European Union members after deciding to leave part of its decommissioned oil rigs standing in the North Sea. Shell argued that removing them would be too costly and risky. Germany said that the estimated 11,000 tonnes of raw oil and toxins remaining in the rigs would eventually seep into the sea, and called it a 'ticking timebomb'.<sup about="#mwt177" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-44" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-44"}}'><a href="#cite_note-44" id="mwAaU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAaY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAac">[</span>44<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAag">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAak">On 15 January 1999, off the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Argentina" title="Argentina" id="mwAao">Argentinian</a> town of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magdalena,_Buenos_Aires" title="Magdalena, Buenos Aires" id="mwAas">Magdalena, Buenos Aires</a>, the Shell tanker <i id="mwAaw">Estrella pampeana</i> collided with a German <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cargo_ship" title="Cargo ship" id="mwAa0">cargo ship</a>, emptying its contents into the lake, polluting the environment, drinkable water, plants and animals. Over a decade after the spill, a referendum held in Magdalena determined the acceptance of a US$9.5<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAa4"> </span>million compensatory payout from Shell.<sup about="#mwt180" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-45" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-45"}}'><a href="#cite_note-45" id="mwAa8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAbA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbE">[</span>45<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbI">]</span></span></a></sup> Shell denied responsibility for the spill, but an Argentine court ruled in 2002 that the corporation was responsible.<sup about="#mwt183" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-46" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-46"}}'><a href="#cite_note-46" id="mwAbM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAbQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbU">[</span>46<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="4" id="mwAbc" aria-labelledby="21st_century"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="21st_century">21st century</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Shell_plc&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4" title="Edit section: 21st century"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAbg"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:ShellgebouwAmsterdam.JPG" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAbk"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:ShellgebouwAmsterdam.JPG" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/ShellgebouwAmsterdam.JPG/250px-ShellgebouwAmsterdam.JPG" decoding="async" data-file-width="1200" data-file-height="1600" data-file-type="bitmap" height="333" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/ShellgebouwAmsterdam.JPG/500px-ShellgebouwAmsterdam.JPG 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAbo"/></a><figcaption id="mwAbs">Former Shell Research and Technology Centre, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amsterdam" title="Amsterdam" id="mwAbw">Amsterdam</a>, c. 2000</figcaption></figure>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAb0"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Shell_Refueller.JPG" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAb4"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Shell_Refueller.JPG" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Shell_Refueller.JPG/250px-Shell_Refueller.JPG" decoding="async" data-file-width="2272" data-file-height="1704" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Shell_Refueller.JPG/500px-Shell_Refueller.JPG 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAb8"/></a><figcaption id="mwAcA">A Shell JET A refueller truck on the ramp at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vancouver_International_Airport" title="Vancouver International Airport" id="mwAcE">Vancouver International Airport</a>, 2005</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAcI">In 2002, Shell acquired <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pennzoil" title="Pennzoil" id="mwAcM">Pennzoil-Quaker State</a> through its American division for US$22 per share, or about US$1.8<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAcQ"> </span>billion. With its acquisition, Shell inherited multiple auto part brands including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jiffy_Lube" title="Jiffy Lube" id="mwAcU">Jiffy Lube</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rain-X" title="Rain-X" id="mwAcY">Rain-X</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fix-a-Flat" title="Fix-a-Flat" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAcc">Fix-a-Flat</a>. The company was notably late in its acquisition as seen by journalists, with Shell seen as streamlining its assets around the same time of other major mergers and acquisitions in the industry, such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BP" title="BP" id="mwAcg">BP</a>'s purchase of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amoco" title="Amoco" id="mwAck">Amoco</a> and the merger of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ExxonMobil" title="ExxonMobil" id="mwAco">Exxon</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mobil" title="Mobil" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAcs">Mobil</a>.<sup about="#mwt186" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-47" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-47"}}'><a href="#cite_note-47" id="mwAcw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAc0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAc4">[</span>47<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAc8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAdA"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Filling_station.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAdE"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Filling_station.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Filling_station.jpg/250px-Filling_station.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="640" data-file-height="482" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Filling_station.jpg/500px-Filling_station.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAdI"/></a><figcaption id="mwAdM">Shell filling station in the UK, 2006</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAdQ">In 2004, Shell overstated its oil reserves, resulting in loss of confidence in the group, a £17<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAdU"> </span>million fine by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Financial_Services_Authority" title="Financial Services Authority" id="mwAdY">Financial Services Authority</a> and the departure of the chairman <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philip_Watts" title="Philip Watts" id="mwAdc">Philip Watts</a>. A lawsuit resulted in the payment of $450<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAdg"> </span>million to non-American shareholders in 2007.<sup about="#mwt189" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-48" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-48"}}'><a href="#cite_note-48" id="mwAdk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAdo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAds">[</span>48<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt192" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-49" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-49"}}'><a href="#cite_note-49" id="mwAd0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAd4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAd8">[</span>49<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt195" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-50" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-50"}}'><a href="#cite_note-50" id="mwAeE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAeI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeM">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAeU">As a result of the scandal, the corporate structure was simplified. Two classes of ordinary shares, A (code RDSA) and B (code RDSB), identical but for the tax treatment of dividends, were issued for the company.<sup about="#mwt198" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-51" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-51"}}'><a href="#cite_note-51" id="mwAeY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAec"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeg">[</span>51<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAek">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAeo"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Shell_Gas_Station_at_Gaya_Street_Sunday_Market,_Kota_Kinabalu_24.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAes"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Shell_Gas_Station_at_Gaya_Street_Sunday_Market,_Kota_Kinabalu_24.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Shell_Gas_Station_at_Gaya_Street_Sunday_Market%2C_Kota_Kinabalu_24.jpg/250px-Shell_Gas_Station_at_Gaya_Street_Sunday_Market%2C_Kota_Kinabalu_24.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="3866" data-file-height="2900" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Shell_Gas_Station_at_Gaya_Street_Sunday_Market%2C_Kota_Kinabalu_24.jpg/500px-Shell_Gas_Station_at_Gaya_Street_Sunday_Market%2C_Kota_Kinabalu_24.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAew"/></a><figcaption id="mwAe0">Shell Gas Station at Gaya Street Sunday Market, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kota_Kinabalu" title="Kota Kinabalu" id="mwAe4">Kota Kinabalu</a>, 2024</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAe8">In November 2004, following a period of turmoil caused by the revelation that Shell had been overstating its <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oil_reserves" title="Oil reserves" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAfA">oil reserves</a>, it was announced that the Shell Group would move to a single capital structure, creating a new parent company to be named Royal Dutch Shell plc, with its primary listing on the LSE, a secondary listing on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euronext_Amsterdam" title="Euronext Amsterdam" id="mwAfE">Euronext Amsterdam</a>, its headquarters and tax residency in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Hague" title="The Hague" id="mwAfI">The Hague</a>, Netherlands and its registered office in London. The company was already incorporated in 2002 as <b id="mwAfM">Forthdeal Limited</b>, a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shelf_corporation" title="Shelf corporation" id="mwAfQ">shelf corporation</a> incorporated by Swift Incorporations Limited and Instant Companies Limited, both based in Bristol.<sup about="#mwt201" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-chshell_52-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"chshell"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-chshell-52"}}'><a href="#cite_note-chshell-52" id="mwAfU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAfY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfc">[</span>52<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfg">]</span></span></a></sup> The unification was completed on 20 July 2005 and the original owners delisted their companies from the respective exchanges.<sup about="#mwt204" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-guardianmay2005_53-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"guardianmay2005"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-guardianmay2005-53"}}'><a href="#cite_note-guardianmay2005-53" id="mwAfk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAfo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfs">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAf0">On 20 July 2005, The "Shell" Transport and Trading Company plc was delisted from the LSE,<sup about="#mwt206" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-54" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-54"}}'><a href="#cite_note-54" id="mwAf4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAf8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgA">[</span>54<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgE">]</span></span></a></sup> changing its name to The Shell Transport and Trading Company Limited<sup about="#mwt209" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-55" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-55"}}'><a href="#cite_note-55" id="mwAgI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAgM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgQ">[</span>55<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgU">]</span></span></a></sup> whereas Royal Dutch Petroleum Company was delisted from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_Stock_Exchange" title="New York Stock Exchange" id="mwAgY">New York Stock Exchange</a> on 18 November 2005.<sup about="#mwt212" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-56" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-56"}}'><a href="#cite_note-56" id="mwAgc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAgg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgk">[</span>56<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgo">]</span></span></a></sup> The shares of the company were issued at a 60/40 advantage for the shareholders of Royal Dutch in line with the original ownership of the Shell Group.<sup about="#mwt214" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-57" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-57"}}'><a href="#cite_note-57" id="mwAgs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAgw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAg0">[</span>57<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAg4">]</span></span></a></sup> The nearly century-old partnership between Royal Dutch Petroleum Company (incorporated in the Netherlands) and The "Shell" Transport and Trading Company plc (incorporated in the United Kingdom) was dissolved. This unification eliminated the previous parent structure and created a single, new holding company incorporated in the United Kingdom: Royal Dutch Shell plc.<sup about="#mwt215" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-guardianmay2005_53-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"guardianmay2005"}}'><a href="#cite_note-guardianmay2005-53" id="mwAg8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAhA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhE">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAhM">During the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Economy_of_Iraq#2009_Oil_services_contracts" title="Economy of Iraq" id="mwAhQ">2009 Iraqi oil services contracts tender</a>, a consortium led by Shell (45%) and which included <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petronas" title="Petronas" id="mwAhU">Petronas</a> (30%) was awarded a production contract for the "Majnoon field" in the south of Iraq, which contains an estimated <span about="#mwt216" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAhY" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"12.6"},"2":{"wt":"Goilbbl"},"3":{"wt":"m3"}},"i":0}}]}'>12.6 billion barrels (2.00</span><span style="margin:0 .15em 0 .25em" about="#mwt216">×</span><span about="#mwt216">10</span><sup about="#mwt216">9</sup><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt216"> </span><span about="#mwt216">m</span><sup about="#mwt216">3</sup><span about="#mwt216">)</span> of oil.<sup about="#mwt219" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-GT-DEX-2009-47_58-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"GT-DEX-2009-47"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-GT-DEX-2009-47-58"}}'><a href="#cite_note-GT-DEX-2009-47-58" id="mwAhc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAhg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhk">[</span>58<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAho">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt223" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-59" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-59"}}'><a href="#cite_note-59" id="mwAhs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAhw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAh0">[</span>59<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAh4">]</span></span></a></sup> The "West Qurna 1 field" production contract was awarded to a consortium led by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ExxonMobil" title="ExxonMobil" id="mwAh8">ExxonMobil</a> (60%) and included Shell (15%).<sup about="#mwt224" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-60" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-60"}}'><a href="#cite_note-60" id="mwAiA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAiE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAiI">[</span>60<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAiM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAiQ">In February 2010, Shell and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cosan" title="Cosan" id="mwAiU">Cosan</a> formed a 50:50 joint-venture, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raízen" title="Raízen" id="mwAiY">Raízen</a>, comprising all of Cosan's Brazilian ethanol, energy generation, fuel distribution and sugar activities, and all of Shell's Brazilian retail fuel and aviation distribution businesses.<sup about="#mwt227" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-61" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-61"}}'><a href="#cite_note-61" id="mwAic"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAig"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAik">[</span>61<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAio">]</span></span></a></sup> In March 2010, Shell announced the sale of some of its assets, including its liquefied petroleum gas (LPG) business, to meet the cost of a planned $28bn capital spending programme. Shell invited buyers to submit indicative bids, due by 22 March, with a plan to raise $2–3bn from the sale.<sup about="#mwt230" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-62" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-62"}}'><a href="#cite_note-62" id="mwAis"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAiw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAi0">[</span>62<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAi4">]</span></span></a></sup> In June 2010, Shell agreed to acquire all the business of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Resources" title="East Resources" id="mwAi8">East Resources</a> for a cash consideration of $4.7<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAjA"> </span>billion. The transaction included East Resources' tight gas fields.<sup about="#mwt233" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-63" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-63"}}'><a href="#cite_note-63" id="mwAjE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAjI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjM">[</span>63<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAjU">Over the course of 2013, the corporation began the sale of its <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shale_gas_in_the_United_States" title="Shale gas in the United States" id="mwAjY">US shale gas</a> assets and canceled a US$20<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAjc"> </span>billion gas project that was to be constructed in the US state of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louisiana" title="Louisiana" id="mwAjg">Louisiana</a>. A new CEO <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ben_van_Beurden" title="Ben van Beurden" id="mwAjk">Ben van Beurden</a> was appointed in January 2014, prior to the announcement that the corporation's overall performance in 2013 was 38 percent lower than in 2012—the value of Shell's shares fell by 3 percent as a result.<sup about="#mwt234" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Tom_64-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Tom"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Tom-64" id="mwAjo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAjs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjw">[</span>64<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAj0">]</span></span></a></sup> Following the sale of the majority of its Australian assets in February 2014, the corporation plans to sell a further US$15<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAj4"> </span>billion worth of assets in the period leading up to 2015, with deals announced in Australia, Brazil and Italy.<sup about="#mwt237" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Bloom_65-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Bloom"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Bloom-65"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Bloom-65" id="mwAj8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAkA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAkE">[</span>65<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAkI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAkM">Shell announced on 8 April 2015 it had agreed to buy <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BG_Group" title="BG Group" id="mwAkQ">BG Group</a> for £47<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAkU"> </span>billion (US$70<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAkY"> </span>billion), subject to shareholder and regulatory approval.<sup about="#mwt240" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-66" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-66"}}'><a href="#cite_note-66" id="mwAkc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAkg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAkk">[</span>66<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAko">]</span></span></a></sup> The acquisition was completed in February 2016, resulting in Shell surpassing <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chevron_Corporation" title="Chevron Corporation" id="mwAks">Chevron Corporation</a> and becoming the world's second largest non-state oil company.<sup about="#mwt243" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Katakey_67-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Katakey"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Katakey-67"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Katakey-67" id="mwAkw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAk0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAk4">[</span>67<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAk8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAlA">On 7 June 2016, Shell announced that it would build an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pennsylvania_Shell_ethane_cracker_plant" title="Pennsylvania Shell ethane cracker plant" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAlE">ethane cracker plant</a> near <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pittsburgh" title="Pittsburgh" id="mwAlI">Pittsburgh</a>, Pennsylvania, after spending several years doing an environmental cleanup of the proposed plant's site.<sup about="#mwt245" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-68" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-68"}}'><a href="#cite_note-68" id="mwAlM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAlQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlU">[</span>68<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAlc">In January 2017, Shell agreed to sell £2.46bn worth of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Sea" title="North Sea" id="mwAlg">North Sea</a> assets to oil exploration firm Chrysaor.<sup about="#mwt248" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-69" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-69"}}'><a href="#cite_note-69" id="mwAlk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAlo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAls">[</span>69<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlw">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2017, Shell sold its <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oil_sands" title="Oil sands" id="mwAl0">oil sands</a> assets to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canadian_Natural_Resources" title="Canadian Natural Resources" id="mwAl4">Canadian Natural Resources</a> in exchange of approximately 8.8% stake in that company. In May 2017, it was reported that Shell plans to sell its shares in Canadian Natural Resources fully exiting the oil sands business.<sup about="#mwt251" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-reuters240517_70-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"reuters240517"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-reuters240517-70"}}'><a href="#cite_note-reuters240517-70" id="mwAl8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAmA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmE">[</span>70<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAmM">On 5 November 2017, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paradise_Papers" title="Paradise Papers" id="mwAmQ">Paradise Papers</a>, a set of confidential <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electronic_document" title="Electronic document" id="mwAmU">electronic documents</a> relating to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Offshore_investment" title="Offshore investment" id="mwAmY">offshore investment</a>, revealed that Argentine Energy Minister <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_José_Aranguren" title="Juan José Aranguren" id="mwAmc">Juan José Aranguren</a> was revealed to have managed the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Offshore_companies" title="Offshore companies" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAmg">offshore companies</a> 'Shell Western Supply and Trading Limited' and 'Sol Antilles y Guianas Limited', both subsidiaries of Shell. One is the main bidder for the purchase of diesel oil by the government through the state owned <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Compañía_Administradora_del_Mercado_Mayorista_Eléctrico_Sociedad_Anónima" title="Compañía Administradora del Mercado Mayorista Eléctrico Sociedad Anónima" id="mwAmk">CAMMESA</a> (Compañía Administradora del Mercado Mayorista Eléctrico).<sup about="#mwt254" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-perfil1_71-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"perfil1"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-perfil1-71"}}'><a href="#cite_note-perfil1-71" id="mwAmo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAms"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmw">[</span>71<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAm0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAm4">On 30 April 2020, Shell announced that it would cut its <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dividend" title="Dividend" id="mwAm8">dividend</a> for the first time since the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_World_War" title="Second World War" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAnA">Second World War</a>, due to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_Russia–Saudi_Arabia_oil_price_war" title="2020 Russia–Saudi Arabia oil price war" id="mwAnE">oil price collapse</a> following the reduction in oil demand during the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/COVID-19_pandemic" title="COVID-19 pandemic" id="mwAnI">COVID-19 pandemic</a>. Shell stated that their net income adjusted for the cost of supply dropped to US$2.9<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAnM"> </span>billion in three months to 31 March. This compared with US$5.3<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAnQ"> </span>billion in the same period the previous year.<sup about="#mwt257" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-72" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-72"}}'><a href="#cite_note-72" id="mwAnU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAnY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnc">[</span>72<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAng">]</span></span></a></sup> On 30 September 2020, the company said that it would cut up to 9,000 jobs as a result of the economic effects caused by the pandemic and announced a "broad restructuring".<sup about="#mwt260" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-73" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-73"}}'><a href="#cite_note-73" id="mwAnk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAno"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAns">[</span>73<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnw">]</span></span></a></sup> In December 2020, Shell forecast another write-down of $3.5–4.5<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAn0"> </span>billion for the fourth quarter due to lower oil prices, following $16.8<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAn4"> </span>billion of impairment in the second quarter.<sup about="#mwt263" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-74" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-74"}}'><a href="#cite_note-74" id="mwAn8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAoA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoE">[</span>74<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAoM">In February 2021, Shell announced a loss of $21.7<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAoQ"> </span>billion in 2020 due to the COVID-19 pandemic,<sup about="#mwt266" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-75" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-75"}}'><a href="#cite_note-75" id="mwAoU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAoY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoc">[</span>75<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAog">]</span></span></a></sup> despite reducing its operating expenses by 12%, or $4.5<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAok"> </span>billion, according to a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morningstar,_Inc." title="Morningstar, Inc." id="mwAoo">Morningstar</a> analysis cited by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barron's_(newspaper)" title="Barron's (newspaper)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAos">Barron's</a>.<sup about="#mwt269" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-76" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-76"}}'><a href="#cite_note-76" id="mwAow"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAo0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAo4">[</span>76<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAo8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt272" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-77" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-77"}}'><a href="#cite_note-77" id="mwApA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwApE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApI">[</span>77<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwApQ">In November 2021, Shell announced that it is planning to relocate their headquarters to London, abandon its dual share structure, and change its name from Royal Dutch Shell plc to Shell plc.<sup about="#mwt275" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-78" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-78"}}'><a href="#cite_note-78" id="mwApU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwApY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApc">[</span>78<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApg">]</span></span></a></sup> The company's name change was registered in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Companies_House" title="Companies House" id="mwApk">Companies House</a> on 21 January 2022.<sup about="#mwt276" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-chshell_52-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"chshell"}}'><a href="#cite_note-chshell-52" id="mwApo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAps"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApw">[</span>52<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAp0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAp4">In December 2021, Shell pulled out of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cambo_oil_field" title="Cambo oil field" id="mwAp8">Cambo oil field</a>, off the Shetland Islands, claiming that "the economic case for investment in this project is not strong enough at this time, as well as having the potential for delays". The proposed oilfield had been the subject of intense campaigning by environmentalists in the run-up to the COP26 UN climate summit in Glasgow in November 2021.<sup about="#mwt279" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-79" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-79"}}'><a href="#cite_note-79" id="mwAqA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAqE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqI">[</span>79<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAqQ">On 4 March 2022, during the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russian_invasion_of_Ukraine" title="Russian invasion of Ukraine" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAqU">Russian invasion of Ukraine</a> and in the midst of the growing <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_boycott_of_Russia_and_Belarus" title="2022 boycott of Russia and Belarus" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAqY">boycott of Russian economy and related divestments</a>, Shell bought a cargo of discounted Russian crude oil.<sup about="#mwt282" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-80" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-80"}}'><a href="#cite_note-80" id="mwAqc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAqg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqk">[</span>80<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqo">]</span></span></a></sup> The next day, following criticism from Ukraine's Foreign Minister <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dmytro_Kuleba" title="Dmytro Kuleba" id="mwAqs">Dmytro Kuleba</a>, Shell defended the purchase as a short term necessity, but also announced that it intended to reduce such purchases, and it would put profits from any Russian oil it purchases into a fund that would go towards humanitarian aid to Ukraine.<sup about="#mwt285" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-81" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-81"}}'><a href="#cite_note-81" id="mwAqw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAq0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAq4">[</span>81<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAq8">]</span></span></a></sup> On 8 March, Shell announced that it would stop buying Russian oil and gas and close its service stations in the country.<sup about="#mwt288" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-82" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-82"}}'><a href="#cite_note-82" id="mwArA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwArE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArI">[</span>82<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwArQ">In 2022, the major oil and gas companies, including Shell,<sup about="#mwt291" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-83" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-83"}}'><a href="#cite_note-83" id="mwArU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwArY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArc">[</span>83<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArg">]</span></span></a></sup> reported sharp rises in interim revenues and profits.<sup about="#mwt294" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-84" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-84"}}'><a href="#cite_note-84" id="mwArk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAro"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArs">[</span>84<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArw">]</span></span></a></sup> In fact, this rise in profit for Shell was so sharp, that 2022 was the company's best year, as Shell recorded double the profits from 2021, and the highest profit in its entire history.<sup about="#mwt297" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-85" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-85"}}'><a href="#cite_note-85" id="mwAr0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAr4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAr8">[</span>85<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAsE">In November 2024, Shell won a case in the Hague court of appeal against <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friends_of_the_Earth" title="Friends of the Earth" id="mwAsI">Friends of the Earth</a> which would have required Shell to cut its carbon emissions by 45%, in line with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_Climate_Accords" title="Paris Climate Accords" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAsM">Paris Climate Accords</a>.<sup about="#mwt300" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-86" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-86"}}'><a href="#cite_note-86" id="mwAsQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAsU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsY">[</span>86<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

